  Object.assign(SIGNIFICATO, {"HAS_FACT": "Committee work on an act read from the summary records: who was heard, opinions, opinions on amendments, steps of the process, answers to questions.", "HAS_DEADLINE": "Deadlines for tabling amendments, sub-amendments and agenda motions to an act in committee: set, moved, expired.", "VOTED": "How a member voted in an electronic vote: in favour, against, abstained, on mission, present not voting.", "SIGNS": "Signature of an amendment: the first signatory (first) or a co-signatory. kind_raw says who files it: a deputy, the rapporteur, the Government.", "SUBJECT": "Topic of the act in the EuroVoc thesaurus, assigned by the Chamber or the Senate.", "SPONSORS": "Who files the act: the first signatory (first) and the co-signatories of a bill, motion or question. When the Government files it, as_office gives the office.", "RAPPORTEUR": "The rapporteur: the member the committee charges with reporting on the act to the floor (majority or minority rapporteur). They did not write it: they present it for the committee.", "HAS_SPEECH": "The speeches on an agenda item, in order.", "BY": "Who gives the speech, with the declared group and the office held at that moment (president, minister, rapporteur).", "HAS_SEGMENT": "The stretches of a speech between reactions, with their position in the text (start, end).", "DURING": "A reaction from the floor (applause, protests) during a speech.", "ADDRESSED_TO": "The ministry a question or interpellation is addressed to.", "HAS_ITEM": "The agenda items of a sitting, in order.", "ON": "The act being voted on: the law, the motion, the resolution.", "HAS_VIDEO": "The stretch of WebTV video showing the speech, with start and end.", "ABOUT": "The act an agenda item deals with.", "HAS_STEP": "The stages of an act's path: filing, assignment, examination, approval.", "FROM": "Where a reaction comes from: the group applauding or protesting.", "HAS_VERSION": "The versions of an act's text: as filed, approved by the committee, approved by the floor.", "ASSIGNED": "Assignment of the act to a committee, with the seat (seat) and the date. Today the outputs only have the lead committee.", "SITS_ON": "Member of a body (committee, junta), with role and dates.", "OFFICE": "An office: president or secretary of a body, group leader, minister, undersecretary, Prime Minister.", "MEMBER_OF": "Membership of a parliamentary group or a Mixed group component, with dates.", "MANDATE": "The parliamentary mandate: Chamber or Senate, constituency, list, election and end dates.", "TRANSMITTED": "The act passing to the other house, with the number it takes there (S. 872).", "JOINED": "Joining: bills on the same topic examined together; text_type marks the base text.", "SAME_AS": "The same person with a record in the Chamber and one in the Senate, matched by first and last name (method).", "PART_OF": "A component inside the Mixed group.", "MENTIONS": "A deputy mentioned in a speech (the link in the bulletin), with the name as written. In Postgres it goes into speech_mention, which will also hold the entities found by NER.", "government": "The government the ministry belongs to.", "sitting": "The sitting where the vote takes place, or that the video shows.", "act": "The act the amendment or text version refers to.", "acts": "The acts the document deals with.", "body": "The body that produced or received the document.", "part_of": "The body it belongs to (a subcommittee within its committee).", "presided_by": "Who presides over the sitting or the vote."});
